.TH OCRECENT 1 "September 2026" "ocrecent 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
ocrecent \- resume recent OpenCode sessions after a reboot
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ocrecent
[\fIflags\fR]
.br
.B ocrecent
\fIcommand\fR [\fIargs\fR] [\fIflags\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B ocrecent
reads the OpenCode SQLite store, ranks sessions by update time, and hands
the newest ones to a picker, a notification, or a direct resume. With no
command and a TTY it opens the picker; otherwise it lists.
.PP
Resume runs
.B opencode <directory> \-\-session <id>
either in-place (TTY) or inside the configured terminal.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B list
List recent sessions.
.TP
.B projects
List recent projects (sessions collapsed by worktree).
.TP
.B pick
Pick a session with the picker and resume it.
.TP
.B resume <id|index>
Resume a session by id or listing index.
.TP
.B last
Resume the most recent session.
.TP
.B print <id|index>
Print the resume command for a session.
.TP
.B notify
Show a notification with pick/projects/last actions.
.TP
.B install
Install user systemd units and XDG autostart entry.
.TP
.B uninstall
Remove them.
.TP
.B doctor
Diagnose store, picker, and environment.
.SH FLAGS
.TP
.BI \-n ", " \-\-max " N"
Maximum number of rows (default 8).
.TP
.B \-\-all
Disable the row limit.
.TP
.B \-\-children
Include subagent (child) sessions.
.TP
.B \-\-archived
Include archived sessions.
.TP
.B \-\-json
Emit JSON on stdout.
.TP
.B \-\-projects
Project grain instead of sessions.
.TP
.BI \-\-picker " BIN"
Picker binary or "auto".
.TP
.BI \-\-dir " DIR"
Only sessions in DIR (or descendants).
.TP
.BI \-\-db " PATH"
Extra database path (repeatable).
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B OPENCODE_DATA
OpenCode data root (containing opencode.db).
.TP
.B OCRECENT_N
Row limit override.
.TP
.B OCRECENT_PICKER
Picker override.
.TP
.B OCRECENT_TERMINAL
Terminal override.
.SH FILES
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/ocrecent/config.toml
\- flat key = value configuration (n, picker, terminal, children, archived,
notify_urgency).
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success, 1 on usage errors or not-found, 2 when the store is
unreadable, 130 when the picker is cancelled.
